@@@!atrep

@@/ at-epistole: the epistolary pack - the frame of a letter
@@/ (ἐπιστολή): whom it is to, how it opens, who signs, and when.
@@/ One symbol family on `-`, each sim its own paragraph.
@@/ Part of the standard library; composes with koine and its
@@/ sibling packs.

@=== addressee
@-: grammata :-@
@"the person a letter is addressed to"@
@""
Own paragraph, at the head of the letter. The person's key rides
as a prosopon aphanes first inside it (@-:@?:(lucilius)Lucilio
suo:-@). A document that is one letter puts it after the front
matter; a collection, at the head of each letter's section.
""@
===@

@=== salutation
@-= grammata =-@
@"the salutation that opens a letter"@
@""
Own paragraph: the letter's own head line ("Dear Sir,"), as the
title is the document's.
""@
===@

@=== signature
@-_ grammata _-@
@"the signature that closes a letter"@
@""
Own paragraph: the line under the letter that attributes it, as
the dialogue tag attributes speech.
""@
===@

@=== composition-date
@-/ grammata /-@
@"composition date at the end of stories or letters"@
@""
Own paragraph. Poems use the verse hypograph instead. Formerly
in at-poesia; the symbol is unchanged.
""@
===@
